<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">The demand for secondary educational facilities continues to outpace supply due to increased college enrollment at a time when existing facilities are becoming more obsolete and traditional funding sources are declining. In addition to classrooms, labs and other campus buildings, many universities are already faced with a significant deficit of student housing. We believe there is a current and growing market for investment opportunities in educational facilities as universities search for equity funding needed to maintain their facilities and meet their growing enrollment. </P>

<H3 STYLE="text-indent:0pt; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; font-weight: bold; text-transform: none; padding-top: 5pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">Acquisition Strategy </H3>

<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">Carter &amp; Associates&#146; higher education practice group has managed approximately $2 billion in new projects and capital improvements through 65 separate projects on 25 campuses. The experience of the team at Carter &amp; Associates ranges from multi-facility capital improvement programs in excess of $100 million to single building and dorm renovations and restorations. Since the group&#146;s inception over 15 years ago, Carter &amp; Associates has maintained a strong reputation by completing every one of its projects on time and with financial savings returned to its clients. Our acquisition strategy will focus on the sourcing of acquisitions,
investments and developments through existing relationships of Carter &amp; Associates with institutions and client referrals, as well as through traditional channels. </P>

