<P STYLE="text-indent:0pt; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">honorary board member of the Georgia State University Department of Real Estate. She also currently is affiliated with the Building Owners and Managers Association, Commercial Real Estate Women, CoreNet Global, Institute of Real Estate Management and International Facility Management. Ms. Hughes obtained a Bachelor of Science from Georgia State University in Atlanta, Georgia in 1994 and a Masters in Business Administration from Georgia State University in Atlanta, Georgia in 1997. </P>

<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B><I>Rutledge Beacham</I></B> is Vice President, Property and Facility Management of Carter Real Estate Management Services, LLC. He joined Carter &amp; Associates in 1978 and currently is its Vice President, Property Management, in which he oversees more than 2.7 million square feet of office, industrial and retail properties. Mr. Beacham has more than 35 years of experience in commercial real estate. He currently is a licensed real estate broker in Georgia, a Real Property Administrator (designated by the Building Owners and Managers Association) and affiliated with the Society of Property Administrators. Mr. Beacham obtained a Bachelor of Science
in Accounting from Georgia State University in Atlanta, Georgia in 1968. </P>

<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B><I>Mike Burson</I></B> is Vice President, Property and Facility Management of Carter Real Estate Management Services, LLC. He joined Carter &amp; Associates in 1992 and currently is its Vice President, Property and Facility Management, in which he leads a 15 million square foot real estate portfolio across multiple markets. Mr. Burson has approximately 30 years of experience in the real estate industry, having served as First Vice President for Resources Property Management Corporation, in which he was responsible for 6 million square feet of commercial real estate in 12 states, and as a Commercial Development Manager for Kaiser Development
Company prior to joining Carter &amp; Associates. He is a Certified Property Manager and a licensed real estate agent in Georgia. Mr. Burson currently is affiliated with the Institute of Real Estate Management and was President of its Atlanta Chapter #67 in 2001, as well as with the Building Owners and Managers Association, National Board of Realtors and the Atlanta Board of Realtors. Mr. Burson obtained a Bachelor in Business Administration from the University of Washington in Seattle, Washington in 1975. </P>

<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B><I>Dena Rodrigues</I></B> is Vice President, Property and Facility Management of Carter Real Estate Management Services, LLC. She joined Carter &amp; Associates in February 2007 and currently is its Vice President, Property and Facility Management. Ms. Rodrigues has more than 20 years of experience in the real estate industry, with an emphasis on portfolio management, lease and contract negotiations and business development. Prior to joining Carter &amp; Associates, she served as Vice President for Jones Lang LaSalle, in which she managed a portfolio of approximately 3 million square feet of commercial office space and worked for CarrAmerica
Realty Corporation, in which she lead operations for a 25 building, 3 million square foot office portfolio and leased and renewed more than 1 million square feet of space each year. She also served on the Georgia Real Estate Commission from 2002 until 2006. Ms. Rodrigues is a Certified Property Manager and a licensed real estate salesperson in Georgia. She also currently serves as Chairman of the Cumberland Area Council and on the Board of Directors of the Cobb Chamber of Commerce, and is affiliated with the Institute of Real Estate Management, an organization for which she formerly served as Vice President of its Atlanta Chapter, the Atlanta Board of Commercial Realtors, the Building Owners and Managers Association and Commercial Real Estate Women. Ms. Rodrigues obtained a Bachelor of Science in Business Education from the University of Tennessee in Knoxville, Tennessee in 1983. </P>

<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">Carter Real Estate Management Services, LLC was organized on December 29, 2009 to lease and manage properties that we or our affiliated entities acquire. In accordance with the property management and leasing agreement, we will pay to our advisor and its affiliates aggregate fees equal to: (a) with respect to single tenant properties, 3.0% of gross revenues from the properties managed; and (b) with respect to multi-tenant properties, 4.0% of gross revenues from the properties managed. Notwithstanding the foregoing, our advisor and its affiliates may be entitled to receive higher fees if our property manager demonstrates to the satisfaction of a
majority of the directors (including a majority of the independent directors) that a higher competitive fee is justified for the services rendered. We also will reimburse the property manager and its affiliates for property-level expenses that they pay or incur on our behalf, including salaries, bonuses and benefits of persons employed by the property manager and its affiliates except for the salaries, bonuses and benefits of persons who also serve as one of our executive officers or as an executive officer of the property manager or its affiliates. The property manager and its affiliates may subcontract the performance of their duties to third parties and pay all or a portion of the property management fee to the third parties with whom they contract for these services. If we contract directly with third parties for such services we will pay them </P>

