          <TD STYLE="padding-left: 10pt; text-indent: -10pt" ROWSPAN=1 COLSPAN=1>Asset Management Fees&nbsp;&#151;&nbsp;Advisor</TD>

          <TD STYLE="width: 12px; vertical-align: text-bottom; text-align: center; border-bottom: none" ROWSPAN=1><!-- GUTTER -->&nbsp;</TD>

          <TD ROWSPAN=1 COLSPAN=1 STYLE="text-align: left">The Company will pay the Advisor a fee equal to 0.75% of the cost of the Company&#146;s assets. (Costs will include the purchase price, acquisition expenses, capital expenditures and other customarily capitalized costs, but exclude acquisition fees). This fee will be payable quarterly in arrears, based on assets held by the Company on the last day of such quarter. The Advisor may elect to have these fees paid, in whole or in part, in cash or in partnership interests in the Operating Partnership (&#147;OP Units&#148;).</TD>

</TR>

<TR STYLE="vertical-align: top">

          <TD STYLE="padding-left: 10pt; text-indent: -10pt" ROWSPAN=1 COLSPAN=1>Property Management and Leasing Fees&nbsp;&#151;&nbsp;Property Manager and Advisor</TD>

          <TD STYLE="width: 12px; vertical-align: text-bottom; text-align: center; border-bottom: none" ROWSPAN=1><!-- GUTTER -->&nbsp;</TD>

          <TD ROWSPAN=1 COLSPAN=1 STYLE="text-align: left">The Company will pay to the Advisor and its affiliates aggregate fees equal to: (a) with respect to single tenant properties, 3.0% of gross revenues from the properties managed; and (b) with respect to multi-tenant properties, 4.0% of gross revenues from the properties managed. The Company will also reimburse the Property Manager and its affiliates for property-level expenses that any of them pay or incur on the Company&#146;s behalf, including salaries, bonuses and benefits of persons employed by the Property Manager and its affiliates except for those persons who also serve as one of the executive officers of the Company or as an executive officer of the Property Manager or its affiliates. The Property Manager and its affiliates may subcontract the performance of their duties to third parties and pay all or a portion of the property management fee to such third parties. If the Company contracts directly with third parties for
such services, the Company will pay a customary market fee and will pay the Property Manager an oversight fee equal to 1.0% of the gross revenues of the property managed. In no event will the Company pay the Property Manger, the Advisor or any affiliate both a property management fee and an oversight fee with respect to any particular property.</TD>

