<H1 STYLE="text-indent:0pt; text-align: center; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: bold; text-transform: none; padding-top: 9pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">CARTER VALIDUS MISSION CRITICAL REIT, INC.<BR>TRANSFER ON DEATH FORM (TOD)<BR> <B><I>This form is NOT VALID for Trust or IRA accounts.</I></B><BR><B>Both pages of this form must accompany the subscription agreement.</B> </H1>

<P STYLE="text-indent:20px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B>As our transfer agent, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;, is located in &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;, a Transfer on Death (&#147;TOD&#148;) designation pursuant to this form and all rights related thereto shall be governed by the laws of the State of &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;.</B> </P>

<P STYLE="text-indent:0pt; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 4px; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><B>PLEASE REVIEW THE FOLLOWING IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE COMPLETING THE TRANSFER ON DEATH FORM:</B> </P>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="text-indent:0px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">

<TR STYLE="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: left">

          <TD STYLE="width: 21px"></TD>

          <TD STYLE="width: 24px; text-align: left">(1)</TD>

          <TD STYLE="text-align: left"><B>Eligible accounts</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;Individual accounts and joint accounts with rights of survivorship are eligible. A TOD designation will not be accepted from residents of Louisiana or North Carolina. </TD>

</TR>

</TABLE>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="text-indent:0px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">

<TR STYLE="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: left">

          <TD STYLE="width: 21px"></TD>

          <TD STYLE="width: 24px; text-align: left">(2)</TD>

          <TD STYLE="text-align: left"><B>Designation of beneficiaries</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;the account owner may designate one or more beneficiaries of the TOD account. Beneficiaries are not &#147;account owners&#148; as the term is used herein. </TD>

</TR>

</TABLE>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="text-indent:0px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">

<TR STYLE="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: left">

          <TD STYLE="width: 21px"></TD>

          <TD STYLE="width: 24px; text-align: left">(3)</TD>

          <TD STYLE="text-align: left"><B>Primary and contingent beneficiaries</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;The account owner may designate primary and contingent beneficiaries of the TOD account. Primary beneficiaries are the first in line to receive the account upon the death of the account owner. Contingent beneficiaries, <I>if any are designated</I>, receive the account upon the death of the account owner if, and only if, there are no surviving primary beneficiaries. </TD>

</TR>

</TABLE>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="text-indent:0px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">

<TR STYLE="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; line-height: 12pt; font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top; text-align: left">

          <TD STYLE="width: 21px"></TD>

          <TD STYLE="width: 24px; text-align: left">(4)</TD>

          <TD STYLE="text-align: left"><B>Minors as beneficiaries</B>:&nbsp;&nbsp;Minors may be beneficiaries of a TOD account only if a custodian, trustee, or guardian is set forth for the minor on the transfer on death form. By not providing a custodian, trustee, or guardian, the account owner is representing that all of the named beneficiaries are not minors. </TD>

</TR>

</TABLE>

<TABLE CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0" WIDTH="100%" STYLE="text-indent:0px; text-align: left; font-family: serif; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; text-transform: none; padding-top: 3pt; padding-right: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt; margin-left: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt">

